      "title": "README: H3 LongTake Image to Video on a song (1.4)",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## H3 LongTake: Image to Video on a song (1.4)\n\n**What it does.** A long video from one picture, clip by clip, moving to a song. Connect the **whole track** to `song` (Load Audio): the node encodes it once and every clip gets its own window — the clip's new audio as `<Audio 1>` and the clip's whole window as an audio guide from frame 0 (`song_mode = both`). It prepends \"The music is the song heard in <Audio 1>.\" to every block: in the blocks ask for movement on the beat.\n\n**Settings.** ref2va + Turbo ref2v 8-step (0.95) + shift 10/3, res_multistep / simple, 8 steps, ~0.5 MP. `song_start_seconds` = where in the song the video starts. `duration_seconds` = how long the video is.\n\n**Output.** The Stitch (active) assembles the clips with the **original song** (saved as song.wav in the project), not the regenerated audio. Refine (muted, Ctrl+M) = second pass at 1 MP, 4 steps, anchored to the previous refined clip; connect the Stitch to its project_dir to assemble the refined video (the song follows).\n\n**Measured** (100 BPM beat, 15 s = 3 clips, 2 seeds): share of the motion on the beat 0.49-0.52 (0.10 on one clip without audio); joins unchanged. Lip sync on a sung track is loose: the model reproduces the song but does not mouth it reliably.\n\nChanging the song or its start = a different plan: mode=restart or a new project_name."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## H3 LongTake: Image to Video on a song (1.4)\n\n**What it does.** A long video from one picture, clip by clip, moving to a song. Connect the **whole track** to `song` (Load Audio): the node encodes it once and every clip gets its own window — the clip's new audio as `<Audio 1>` and the clip's whole window as an audio guide from frame 0 (`song_mode = both`). It prepends \"The music is the song heard in <Audio 1>.\" to every block: in the blocks ask for movement on the beat.\n\n**Settings.** ref2va + Turbo ref2v 8-step (0.95) + shift 10/3, res_multistep / simple, 8 steps, ~0.5 MP. `song_start_seconds` = where in the song the video starts. `duration_seconds` = how long the video is.\n\n**Output.** The Stitch (active) assembles the clips with the **original song** (saved as song.wav in the project), not the regenerated audio. Refine (muted, Ctrl+M) = second pass at 1 MP, 4 steps, anchored to the previous refined clip; connect the Stitch to its project_dir to assemble the refined video (the song follows).\n\n**Measured** (100 BPM beat, 15 s = 3 clips, 2 seeds): share of the motion on the beat 0.49-0.52 (0.10 on one clip without audio); joins unchanged. Lip sync on a sung track is loose: the model reproduces the song but does not mouth it reliably.\n\nChanging the song or its start = a different plan: mode=restart or a new project_name."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
